# The clip batches, which are carried OUT OF BAND rather than in the repo — they
# are ~1.5 GB across eight parallel copies of the same 40 clips (one per
# super-resolution experiment, so ?sr=<key> can A/B them; see VIDEO_SR in
# src/Tour.jsx). None of them has ever been tracked. Listed explicitly because
# they are not obviously generated, so a `git add -A` would otherwise commit the
# lot, and because /video-plain now holds all 39 remuxed fallback clips rather
# than the two it used to.
#
# A deploy needs these present: `best` serves from video-latest2, video-latest,
# video-x4 and video-fit, with video-plain as the fallback root. Copy them in
# before building; the build drops the A/B-only roots and prunes the fallback
# (see vite.config.js).
/public/video-2x/
/public/video-fit/
/public/video-latest/
/public/video-latest2/
/public/video-plain/
/public/video-x4/
/public/video-x4-48/

# Raw art out of the generation pipeline: the full-size MJ candidates and their
# working files. What the tour actually serves is the WebP derived from them and
# committed under public/nodes/.
source-assets/
